1
00:00:00,306 --> 00:00:05,135
Run the same suite with the new test
present. Look for the zero test name and

2
00:00:05,135 --> 00:00:06,257
the assertion message.

3
00:00:06,826 --> 00:00:11,322
True was returned where false was
expected. That failure supports the

4
00:00:11,322 --> 00:00:12,119
hypothesis.

5
00:00:12,709 --> 00:00:15,398
If the suite stops because of a missing
import,

6
00:00:15,744 --> 00:00:17,987
it hasn't shown that the boundary is
wrong.

7
00:00:18,578 --> 00:00:22,917
Fix the setup first and rerun until you
have the failure you intended to test.

8
00:00:24,742 --> 00:00:27,905
Change greater than or equal to zero to
greater than zero.

9
00:00:28,218 --> 00:00:31,791
Keep the assertion and the function
signature as they are.

10
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:35,023
Rerun the same test command on the
updated checkout.

11
00:00:35,358 --> 00:00:39,617
Now all four cases should pass. Check
the source diff and the test diff

12
00:00:39,617 --> 00:00:40,267
together.

13
00:00:40,527 --> 00:00:43,734
Each one should answer a part of the
issue you started with.
